<node>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="An integer is a datum of integral data type, a data type that represents some range of mathematical integers.
It is allowed to contain negative values.

The standard type used internally is int with 32 Bits.
It has a value range from −2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647, which is from −(2^31) to 2^31 - 1.

Each number can be an element of a vector (array), e.g.:
- integer: 1,2,3,4"/>
    <node name="examples" channel="file" format="text/plain" model="api-generator/spec/state/number/integer/examples.txt"/>
</node>
